# vitepress
docs/.vitepress/dist/
docs/.vitepress/cache/

# complykit run artifacts. Runs and the verdict cache are per-machine and
# regenerable; the route manifest and dispositions are tracked deliberately
# (build-plan §7). Test fixtures under test/ are NOT ignored.
.comply/runs/
.comply/cache/

# A bare `config.js`/`config.ts` rule in a user's global gitignore
# (core.excludesFile) applies to every repo on the machine. It silently dropped
# both an adapter module and the docs config from featureboard's first push —
# CI caught the first, nothing caught the second (VitePress builds fine without
# a config and deploys a site with no nav). Repo rules outrank the global file,
# so these are re-included explicitly. See standards/traps.md #1.
!src/**/config.js
!src/**/config.ts
!docs/.vitepress/config.js
!docs/.vitepress/config.ts
